# Cursor IDE Rules for JanSeva Project

You are working on JanSeva (West Bengal AI Public Support System) — a Next.js 16 + Supabase + n8n project for citizen grievances and blood donor matching.

## ALWAYS Read First
- `PROJECT_CONTEXT.md` — Full project bootstrap
- `AGENTS.md` — AI working rules
- `.ai-context/CURRENT_STATE.md` — Current focus
- `.kiro/specs/sahayak-multi-agent-router/requirements.md` — Active spec

## Tech Stack
- Next.js 16, React, TypeScript (strict), Tailwind, shadcn/ui
- Supabase (PostgreSQL 17, Auth, Storage, Realtime)
- Prisma ORM
- n8n self-hosted (workflows prefixed `JS-`)
- Google Gemini for LLM
- WhatsApp Business API

## Code Style
- Strict TypeScript — no `any`
- Server Components by default; mark `'use client'` only when needed
- Tailwind utility classes; reuse shadcn/ui components
- Conventional Commits: `feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:`, `docs:`, `refactor:`, `test:`
- Imports: external → internal (`@/*`) → types
- Error handling: try/catch with structured logging

## Critical Rules
1. NEVER hardcode secrets — use `process.env.X` and `.env.example`
2. NEVER delete from `donation_history` — immutable audit trail
3. ALWAYS use cascade engine (JS-15B) for blood donor notifications — never broadcast directly
4. ALWAYS run pre-donation health screening before marking donor accepted
5. ALWAYS check `conversation_sessions.last_intent` for routing — never let the LLM guess
6. Mask donor phone numbers in non-admin views (e.g., `98XXX XX234`)
7. Medical compliance per Indian NACO/NBTC + WHO guidelines

## File Structure
- `src/app/` — Next.js App Router (pages + API routes)
- `src/app/api/` — API endpoints, organized by resource
- `src/components/` — React components
- `src/components/ui/` — shadcn/ui components
- `src/hooks/` — React hooks
- `src/lib/` — utilities, Supabase client, helpers
- `prisma/` — Prisma schema and migrations
- `n8n-workflows/` — n8n workflow JSON definitions
- `n8n-sdk-v3/` — n8n deployment SDK
- `.ai-context/` — Documentation for AI tools
- `.kiro/specs/` — Active feature specs
- `skills/` — Reusable code generation patterns

## Naming
- n8n workflows: `JS-NN: Name` (e.g., `JS-01: Sahayak Multi-Agent`)
- Ticket IDs: `WB-YYYY-XXXXX` (e.g., `WB-2026-00123`)
- DB tables: `snake_case`, plural (`blood_donors`)
- Components: `PascalCase` (`ComplaintCard.tsx`)
- API routes: `/api/<resource>/<action>` (`/api/complaints/register`)

## Build / Test
```bash
npm run dev      # development
npm run build    # production build
npm run lint     # eslint
```

## Communication
- WhatsApp messages: Hinglish + Bengali support, conversational
- UI: English primary with Bengali/Hindi translations on citizen pages
- Code/docs: English
- Comments: explain WHY, not WHAT

## When Implementing New Features
1. Check active spec in `.kiro/specs/`
2. Match existing patterns in `src/`
3. Add to `.ai-context/CURRENT_STATE.md`
4. Run lint + build before committing
5. Push to feature branch (`feat/<name>`)
